    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0063" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v23p2/pg35"/>

                <head>19. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Switzerland<anchor n="1" xml:id="d19-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-02-11T16:05:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                                1955—4:05 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1066. Tokyo also pass CINCUNC. Our 510 to
                    Seoul repeated Bern 1052 Stockholm 591 and Tokyo 1583.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d19-f2"/> Department officers met separately Swiss and Swedish
                    representatives February 10.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d19-f3"/> Explained Sixteen
                    believed unlikely Communists agree preferred alternative liquidation NNSC but some indication Communists might accept
                    some form reduction personnel. Sixteen therefore hope Swiss and Swedes make
                    available on confidential basis detailed proposals reduction personnel NNSC for discussion with Sixteen February 18.
                    Swiss and Swedish representatives agreed make this request their governments.
                    Also agreed put to their governments question possible desirability asking
                    Chinese Communists reaction aide-mémoire.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 795.00/2–1155. Secret. Drafted by
                        Jones, cleared with EUR
                    and UNP, and approved by McClurkin. Also sent to Stockholm and
                    repeated to Seoul and Tokyo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f2" n="2" xml:id="d19-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f3" n="3" xml:id="d19-f3-content">
                <p>Memoranda of these conversations are in Department of State, Central Files,
                    795.00/2–1055.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
